                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Where does ITD GrowthLabs fit in the jewelry agency landscape?</h3>
                                        <p>Category-broad D2C agency with proven jewelry vertical track record. Fabelia case study + 8+ published jewelry playbooks + 6 GCC city-specific pages + Rs 8Cr+ annual managed ad spend. India + GCC dual-market with trilingual creative. 3-tier pricing (Starter Rs 75K / Growth Rs 2L / Enterprise Rs 5L+) + ad-spend transparent pass-through billing.</p>
                                        <h3>When is ITD not the best fit for a jewelry brand?</h3>
                                        <p>Pure luxury + heritage-designer at Rs 25 lakh+ AOV (evaluate luxury sub-vertical specialist alongside us). Hyper-boutique launches under Rs 25L / month revenue (may fit better with founder + freelancer collective at lower cost). Rs 500 Cr+ enterprise with in-house team + marquee celebrity + Vogue-tier PR ambition (evaluate luxury boutique specialist).</p>
                                        <h3>What are the main category-broad D2C agencies competing in jewelry?</h3>
                                        <p>Enterprise: Kinnect + Schbang + large FMCG + D2C agencies (Rs 3-15L / month, typically bundled ad-spend). Performance-heavy: Sokrati + Performics-scale (Rs 2-10L / month). Full-service: WATconsult + Grapes Digital-tier (Rs 2-8L / month). Boutique: Everest Brand Solutions + smaller (Rs 1-5L / month). ITD sits between with transparent pricing + jewelry specialisation.</p>
                                        <h3>What are jewelry sub-vertical specialists and when do they win?</h3>
                                        <p>Sub-vertical specialists focus on one segment: luxury + heritage-designer (Rs 25L+ AOV brands), bridal + wedding-jewelry (deep bridal-blogger + wedding-planner network), regional-heritage (temple + kundan + Bengali traditional), lab-grown diamond (emerging category education + certification). Excel in specific segment but lack breadth for adjacency expansion without switching agencies.</p>
                                        <h3>How should we choose between category-broad and sub-vertical specialist?</h3>
                                        <p>Fashion + everyday-luxe + men's + emerging fine + Rs 25L-25 Cr / month: category-broad. Bridal-focused Rs 2-25 Cr / month: evaluate both (bridal specialist OR category-broad with strong bridal case studies). Pure luxury + celebrity + Vogue-tier ambition: luxury sub-vertical specialist. Multi-region enterprise: category-broad with proven multi-region.</p>
                                        <h3>What matters most in agency evaluation?</h3>
                                        <p>Named jewelry client work + live URLs + attribution transparency + ad-spend billing model (transparent pass-through vs bundled markup) + team + founder access + reporting cadence. See our <a href="/resources/best_digital_marketing_agency_jewelry_brands_india.php">12-point evaluation framework</a> + <a href="/resources/jewelry_marketing_agency_portfolio_red_flags.php">portfolio red flags</a> guide.</p>
                                        <h3>Should we always shortlist 3-5 agencies before signing?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes. Systematic 6-week shortlist process: research 15-25 candidates + score on 12-point framework + shortlist top 5-8 + discovery calls + scoped proposals from top 3 + reference checks with past jewelry clients + select + 6-month MSA with month-to-month cancellation after month 3.</p>
                                        <h3>How do we validate ITD's claims + fit vs alternatives?</h3>
                                        <p>Book a 30-min discovery call via our <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-jewelry-brands.php">jewelry vertical page</a>. Full portfolio + client references (under NDA) + scoped proposal with 90-day plan + budget + KPIs + team + timeline within 3 business days. Compare against 2-4 alternative agencies + choose based on fit + evidence + transparency.</p>
